// native-turn-run.bml — one engineering turn by the body's own loop: a queued gap, the native code lane, the band.
//
// Reads learn/native-turn-queue.jsonl (id, goal, writable, band, full, and optionally document_context "catalog"
// for a writable file larger than the voice's context) and takes the open gap with the fewest
// attempts in receipts/native-turn-ledger.jsonl. A gap whose latest real row is the lane's rung-0 refusal
// (caller-check-unmeetable) under the contract the queue and the tree still hold (its checks and the texts of its
// documents) waits on that contract, and the walk's own pick passes it by; a changed check or a healed source opens
// it, and a gap asked for by name is taken. A gap whose every way the ladder's gate refuses under its contract (each
// way's approach already stands with a non-green outcome) waits the same way, so its turn is never opened to print
// nothing. Runs the gap's band as a cell called in this process (cell_run); when it already
// reads full the turn records that reading and the gap stays closed. No model runs. A band that read above its full, or whose own "; Verdict n"
// head names another verdict than the gap's full, cannot be met: the turn lands one row (rung "contract", lane_reason
// "band-above-full" or "band-head-differs") and opens no option, and the gap waits on its contract (its checks, the
// texts of its documents, its band and its full). That row is a ledger row, not a turn: an unnamed real turn goes on
// to the next open gap in the same window (the walk line names what the turn parked), so the cheapest refusal in
// the ladder costs no window; asked for by name, or run as a dry or test turn, it prints the row and ends.
// Otherwise the turn is a backtrack walk (oac-backtrack-walk,
// control/choice-lane-core.fk) over the ladder's ways (form-stdlib/bml/native-turn-ladder.bml), each a distinct
// approach, with a caller-sized allowance of local model attempts (six by default). The ways, in order: native (rung 0,
// no model: the body's own boolean-syntax repair and one-value wrapper search against the band, at most 16 band
// runs inside twenty minutes), first, resume, context, lens, voice. The model ways hand the goal to the native code
// lane in this same process (fcaq-decoded: the request and the result stay nodes; local Qwen, no rented fallback) with the writable sources
// as documents and the gap's own read-only checks, then run the band again; every request also carries
// native_rehearsal_checks (16), so the lane's own rehearsal after a failed or unchanged action is on in every turn.
// A way whose approach digest already stands under this contract (the gap's checks and the texts of its documents,
// its band and its full) with a non-green outcome is refused with no option (no GPU; the refusal is kept in the
// walk's memory, and no finding of its own reaches the next way), so a later walk starts at the first way not yet
// read; a resume is admitted again only while the outcomes move. A row the walk stopped (the lane at the deadline, a
// lane that never launched, the native rung at the window's end, a publish refused, a tree that moved) judged
// nothing and is no history. A refusal prints "[native-turn:clinamen] <gap> <rung> refused: <why>", and the walk
// line carries "; refused: <rung> <why's kind>, ..." because the host keeps a turn's last row and walk line only.
// An option whose band did not turn green is a backtrack point, not an end: it keeps its candidate under
// .hearth/native-turns, and acks a node carrying what it saw (the band's reading, the lane's status, the candidate's
// diff, and the compiler's own words when the band ran under the candidate and did not read). The candidate stands
// in the tree only inside hw-with-published (form-stdlib/bml/host-walk.bml), over the tree as it stands after the
// lane (absence included, so a writable path the lane creates publishes and is gone again after the window): a marker
// read back first, the restore deferred, so a stop restores the source and a kill leaves a marker the next start
// heals. A publish the door refuses ran no band: its row keeps band_after where the band was, its finding carries no
// compiler words, and, like a source that moved during generation, it ends the walk. The resume way resumes the
// checkpoint of the last option (this walk's, else the ledger's under the same contract that its own model opened) under the unchanged original
// request, with that finding as an identified feedback event; the context, lens and voice ways open a fresh
// checkpoint and carry the finding as text beside the goal. A green option keeps its edit for the landing and ends
// the walk. Each option lands its own row: gap, option, band before and after (null when the band printed no number),
// full, band_green, the lane's reason and blocking check, the digests of the contract it ran under (checks_digest:
// checks and document texts; band_digest: band text and full), the session that
// began it when the caller names one, and who began the turn, read from the host's own process table; and the ladder's
// fields: rung, approach, approach_digest, outcome_digest, clinamen (what differs from the nearest earlier
// approach), finding, stillstreak_max and remote_dependence. The native row carries no wall_ms (it is not a model
// option) and a known 0 local IDs. Coordinator identity is attribution, not token usage; unmeasured rented
// tokens remain null.
// The wall deadline: {"deadline_ms":<host_monotonic_ms>} (the walk's window end). No option starts once the time
// left cannot hold the walk's option floor (hw-option-floor). A deadline already past opens no generation: the row
// reads lane "lane-deadline" and lane_reason "deadline". A generation in flight ends on the lane's own turn budget,
// a memory return, or the walk's child backstop. The band still runs in its own kernel and stops at the earlier of
// its ten minutes and the deadline. With no deadline the lane runs to its end. A lane that gave its memory back because the machine ran low (lane_reason "host-memory-low", the lane saved
// its checkpoint first: form-cli-code-live.bml fcac-memory-stop), or whose session open was refused for memory
// ("host-memory-held:<why>"), is a choice point, not a failed option (mg-memory-ending?): it spends no option
// (nt-spent, nt-attempts), ends the walk there (the machine is short for every way), the host walk reads it as neither
// idle nor unknown (hw-memory-low?), the ladder reads it as an interrupted row (no tried approach), and a later walk
// resumes its checkpoint (the pending row ntl-hist-of leaves: the resume way takes it and hears only that nothing
// failed, ntl-feedback-text; the first way waits for it). A lane whose seat was already taken (lane_reason
// "model-queued: ...") is the same choice: nothing opened, the option is not spent, the walk ends (every later way
// would wait on the same seat), and the ladder keeps the approach open.
// A test turn ({"test":1}) writes its rows to .hearth/native-turns/test-ledger.jsonl and always restores the
// source, so a turn begun by a session can learn what the lane can do without closing a gap the nights must close.
// {"publish_from":"<lane output>"} publishes a result already on disk instead of asking the lane (a test of the path);
// {"candidate":"<file>"} publishes that file's text as the gap's first writable document (a test of one candidate).
// stdin, optional: {"gap":"<id>","dry":1,"test":1,"model":"qwen38-q8","context":16384,"turns":64,"attempts":6,
// "deadline_ms":0,"session":"<the caller's session id>","ways":["native","first"],"queue":"<queue file>",
// "ledger":"<ledger file>"}; dry skips the lane and the native
// rung's band runs; ways keeps only the named rungs of the ladder (a test of one rung); queue reads another queue
// file than learn/native-turn-queue.jsonl and ledger reads and writes another ledger file than
// receipts/native-turn-ledger.jsonl (a test of a scratch gap; form-stdlib/tests/native-turn-ladder-band.bml runs
// the door so).
// preflight-exec: forbidden
import form-stdlib/bml/host-walk.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-task.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/cell-said.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/native-turn-ladder.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-task-runtime.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-code-request.bml;
import form-stdlib/model-registry.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-heal-native-report.bml;
import form-stdlib/meaning-codes.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/parse.bml;
import control/offer-ack-core.fk;
import control/choice-lane-core.fk;
import form-stdlib/bml/text-diff.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/stdin-source.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/live.bml;
import form-stdlib/bml/form-agent-json-query.bml;
section [form.bml] {
 class NativeTurn {
  def nt-queue() = "learn/native-turn-queue.jsonl";
  def nt-ledger() = "receipts/native-turn-ledger.jsonl";
  def nt-dir() = hw-turn-dir();
  def nt-str(doc, key) = if json-object-has?(doc, key) then json-string-value(json-object-get(doc, key)) else "";
  def nt-int(doc, key, d) = if json-object-has?(doc, key) then json-int-value(json-object-get(doc, key)) else d;
  def nt-maybe(doc,key) = !json-object-has?(doc,key) || node_eq(json-object-get(doc,key),json-node-null()) ? nothing() : json-int-value(json-object-get(doc,key));
  def nt-strs(doc, key) = if json-object-has?(doc, key) then nt-values(json-array-elements(json-object-get(doc, key))) else [];
  def nt-values(nodes) = if nil?(nodes) then [] else cons(json-string-value(nodes[0]), nt-values(nodes[1:]));
  def nt-nonempty(xs) = if nil?(xs) then [] else if ((Comparable) len(trim(xs[0])) == 0) then nt-nonempty(xs[1:]) else cons(xs[0], nt-nonempty(xs[1:]));
  def nt-parse(xs) = if nil?(xs) then [] else cons(parse-json("native-turn-row", xs[0]), nt-parse(xs[1:]));
  def nt-rows(path) = if (file_size(path) < 1) then [] else nt-parse(nt-nonempty(split-on(fhn-read(path), "\n")));
  def nt-green?(id, rows) = if nil?(rows) then 0 else if (((String) nt-str(rows[0], "gap") == id) && ((Comparable) nt-int(rows[0], "band_green", 0) == 1)) then 1 else nt-green?(id, rows[1:]);
  // the open gap with the fewest real attempts, in queue order among equals, so one gap the lane cannot yet
  // close does not hold the others
  // an attempt is a row that tried something: a lane that gave its memory back, was refused it, or found the seat taken, tried nothing
  def nt-untried?(reason) = mg-memory-ending?(reason) || ntl-queued?(reason);
  def nt-attempts(id, rows) = if nil?(rows) then 0 else ((if (((String) nt-str(rows[0], "gap") == id) && ((Comparable) nt-int(rows[0], "dry", 0) == 0) && (!nt-untried?(nt-str(rows[0], "lane_reason")))) then 1 else 0) + nt-attempts(id, rows[1:]));
  // the contract a gap runs under, read as one number: the queue row's checks, emitted canonically, and the text of
  // every document the lane reads for it (nt-sources: its writable files and its read-only sources, a path not there
  // read as its absence), folded. A check's witness reads those documents, so a source healed on main is a new
  // contract as surely as a changed check.
  def nt-digest-from(s, i, n, d) = if (i >= n) then d else nt-digest-from(s, (i + 1), n, (((d * 131) + str_byte_at(s, i)) % 2147483647));
  def nt-digest(s) = nt-digest-from(s, 0, len(s), 7).str();
  def nt-source-texts(paths) = if nil?(paths) then "" else mc-cat(["\n", paths[0], "\n", read_file(paths[0]) ?? "(absent)", nt-source-texts(paths[1:])]);
  def nt-checks-digest(gap) = nt-digest(mc-cat([json-emit(if json-object-has?(gap, "checks") then json-object-get(gap, "checks") else json-node-array([])), nt-source-texts(nt-sources(gap))]));
  // a gap waits on its contract when its latest real row (not dry, not a test) is the lane's rung-0 refusal under
  // the contract the queue and the tree still hold; a new check, or a healed one or a healed source, opens it again.
  // The digest is read only for a gap whose latest real row is that refusal.
  def nt-real?(row) = (((Comparable) nt-int(row, "dry", 0) == 0) && ((Comparable) nt-int(row, "test", 0) == 0));
  def nt-latest-real(id, rows, found) = if nil?(rows) then found else nt-latest-real(id, rows[1:], if (((String) nt-str(rows[0], "gap") == id) && nt-real?(rows[0])) then [rows[0]] else found);
  def nt-unmeetable-reason() = "caller-check-unmeetable";
  def nt-refused?(row) = ((String) nt-str(row, "lane_reason") == nt-unmeetable-reason());
  // a gap whose band cannot be met (read above its full, or its own head names another verdict) waits on the band
  // and the full as well: the band's text and the gap's full are the contract that refusal read
  def nt-band-digest(gap) = nt-digest(mc-cat([read_file(nt-str(gap, "band")) ?? "(absent)", "\n", nt-int(gap, "full", 0).str()]));
  def nt-band-refused?(row) = fcgp-member?(ntl-contract-reasons(), nt-str(row, "lane_reason"));
  // A gap whose every way the gate refuses under its contract waits on that contract too: its walk would open no
  // option and print no row, and the window would end on a turn that took nothing. The gate's own reading
  // (nt-way-verdict) over the rows the walk's gate reads (nt-ledger-rows); only a gap that holds a ladder row can be
  // refused, so a gap with none costs no reading of its documents.
  def nt-has-ladder-rows?(id, rows) = any?(r => ((String) nt-str(r, "gap") == id) && ((Comparable) len(nt-str(r, "approach_digest")) > 0), rows);
  def nt-stands?(gap, opts) {
   let rows = nt-ledger-rows(opts);
   if (!nt-has-ladder-rows?(nt-str(gap, "id"), rows)) then false
   else {
    let hist = ntl-hist-of(rows, nt-str(gap, "id"), nt-checks-digest(gap), nt-band-digest(gap));
    nil?(filter(way => (Comparable) nt-way-verdict(way, gap, [], hist)[0] == 1, nt-ways-of(gap, opts)));
   };
  }
  def nt-waits?(gap, done, opts) {
   let last = nt-latest-real(nt-str(gap, "id"), done, []);
   let parked = nil?(last) ? false : nt-refused?(last[0]) ? ((String) nt-str(last[0], "checks_digest") == nt-checks-digest(gap)) : nt-band-refused?(last[0]) ? (((String) nt-str(last[0], "checks_digest") == nt-checks-digest(gap)) && ((String) nt-str(last[0], "band_digest") == nt-band-digest(gap))) : false;
   parked || nt-stands?(gap, opts);
  }
  // A queue row is a gap when it names itself and names a band or a goal. A verified task record in the same file is not a turn.
  def nt-gap?(row) = ((String) nt-str(row, "id") != "") && (((String) nt-str(row, "band") != "") || ((String) nt-str(row, "goal") != ""));
  def nt-open(queue, done, want, opts) = if nil?(queue) then [] else if (nt-gap?(queue[0]) && (((String) want == "") || ((String) nt-str(queue[0], "id") == want)) && ((Comparable) nt-green?(nt-str(queue[0], "id"), done) == 0) && (((String) want != "") || !nt-waits?(queue[0], done, opts))) then cons(queue[0], nt-open(queue[1:], done, want, opts)) else nt-open(queue[1:], done, want, opts);
  def nt-waiting(queue, done, opts) = if nil?(queue) then [] else if (((Comparable) nt-green?(nt-str(queue[0], "id"), done) == 0) && nt-waits?(queue[0], done, opts)) then cons(nt-str(queue[0], "id"), nt-waiting(queue[1:], done, opts)) else nt-waiting(queue[1:], done, opts);
  def nt-none-open(queue, done, opts) {
   let waiting = nt-waiting(queue, done, opts);
   if nil?(waiting) then "[native-turn] no open gap" else mc-cat(["[native-turn] no open gap: ", nt-comma(waiting), " wait(s) on its contract (the lane refused a caller check no candidate can meet, the band reads above its full or names another verdict than its full, or every way of the ladder already stands with a non-green outcome; and nothing that contract reads has changed since)"]);
  }
  def nt-least(gaps, done, best) = if nil?(gaps) then best else nt-least(gaps[1:], done, if (nil?(best) || (nt-attempts(nt-str(gaps[0], "id"), done) < nt-attempts(nt-str(best[0], "id"), done))) then [gaps[0]] else best);
  def nt-pick(queue, done, want, opts) = nt-least(nt-open(queue, done, want, opts), done, []);
  // a band reads its number only when its run exits 0 with a number on its last line; anything else is a fold
  // over nothing and reads nothing (axiom-1), never a number and never a -1 code. The run is a live step
  // (form-stdlib/bml/live.bml), spoken as it lands against the gap's full; a band short of full needs code,
  // and the repair that meets it is this turn's own walk through the lane. The compiler's own error lines
  // stay beside the reading.
  def nt-out() = mc-cat([nt-dir(), "/band.out"]);
  def nt-err() = mc-cat([nt-dir(), "/band.err"]);
  // A candidate may loop; the band answers within its deadline or reads nothing, so one
  // looping candidate cannot hold the night's turns. With a wall deadline (the walk's window end) the band also
  // stops there: the earlier of ten minutes from its start and the deadline.
  def nt-band-deadline-ms() = 600000;
  def nt-band-until(deadline, now) = ((Comparable) deadline > 0) && (deadline < (now + nt-band-deadline-ms())) ? deadline : now + nt-band-deadline-ms();
  // The band is a cell called in this process (cell_run: no child, no exit to wait for), with the budget the turn gives it
  // (nt-band-until) as its deadline. It reads a number only when the cell ran to its end with no compile error and ended on
  // an integer; its evidence stands where the turn reads it: band.out holds what it printed and the value it ended on,
  // band.err what it said (the compiler's lines, the live readings its claims voiced).
  def nt-band-left(deadline, now) = nt-band-until(deadline, now) - now < 1 ? 1 : nt-band-until(deadline, now) - now;
  def nt-band-ran?(rec) = !nothing?(rec) && nothing?(record_get(rec, "stopped")) && ((Comparable) record_get(rec, "errors") == 0);
  def nt-band-number(v) = (String) value_kind(v) == "int" ? v : (String) value_kind(v) == "string" ? parse-int(trim(v)) : nothing();
  def nt-band-keep(rec) {
   let wrote = write_file_text(nt-out(), cs-stdout(rec));
   write_file_text(nt-err(), cs-stderr(rec) ++ (nothing?(rec) || nothing?(record_get(rec, "stopped")) ? "" : "fkwu: " ++ (String) record_get(record_get(rec, "stopped"), "message") ++ "\n"));
  }
  def nt-band-run(ctx) {
   let rec = cell_run(ctx[0], 0, nt-band-left(ctx[2], host_monotonic_ms()), nothing());
   let kept = nt-band-keep(rec);
   nt-band-ran?(rec) ? nt-band-number(record_get(rec, "value")) : nothing();
  }
  def nt-full?(value, ctx) = if nothing?(value) then false else ((Comparable) value == ctx[1]);
  def nt-band(path, full, deadline) {
   let made = fs_mkdir(nt-dir());
   let heard = host_path_remove(nt-err());
   live-do("native-turn", path, [path, full, deadline], nt-band-run, nt-full?, [])[1];
  }
  def nt-read(path) = if (file_size(path) < 1) then "" else fhn-read(path);
  def nt-starts?(s, p) = ((len(s) >= len(p)) && ((String) substring(s, 0, len(p)) == p));
  def nt-error-lines(lines, n) = if (nil?(lines) || (n <= 0)) then [] else if ((str_find(lines[0], "error", 0) >= 0) && (!nt-starts?(lines[0], "form-organ"))) then cons(substring(lines[0], 0, if (len(lines[0]) > 300) then 300 else len(lines[0])), nt-error-lines(lines[1:], (n - 1))) else nt-error-lines(lines[1:], n);
  def nt-band-errors() = trim(nt-join(nt-error-lines(split-on(nt-read(mc-cat([nt-dir(), "/band.err"])), "\n"), 6)));
  // A band whose claims are live steps (form-stdlib/bml/live.bml) speaks each as an organ-health reading on
  // stderr. The steps whose last reading did not hold are the backtracking signal the next option hears:
  // what each answered, and the repairs the band already tried in its own run.
  def nt-health-prefix() = "form-organ health ";
  def nt-band-rows(lines) = if nil?(lines) then [] else if (nt-starts?(lines[0], nt-health-prefix()) && (str_find(lines[0], "\"organ\":\"live\"", 0) >= 0)) then cons(parse-json("band-reading", substring(lines[0], len(nt-health-prefix()), len(lines[0]))), nt-band-rows(lines[1:])) else nt-band-rows(lines[1:]);
  def nt-row-str(row, key) = if json-object-has?(row, key) then json-string-value(json-object-get(row, key)) else "";
  def nt-observe?(row) = ((String) nt-row-str(row, "stage") == "observe");
  def nt-aspects(rows, seen) = if nil?(rows) then reverse(seen) else nt-aspects(rows[1:], if (nt-observe?(rows[0]) && ((Comparable) nt-has(seen, nt-row-str(rows[0], "aspect")) == 0)) then cons(nt-row-str(rows[0], "aspect"), seen) else seen);
  def nt-last-observed(rows, aspect, found) = if nil?(rows) then found else nt-last-observed(rows[1:], aspect, if (nt-observe?(rows[0]) && ((String) nt-row-str(rows[0], "aspect") == aspect)) then rows[0] else found);
  def nt-tried(rows, aspect) = nt-tried-go(rows, aspect, []);
  def nt-tried-go(rows, aspect, seen) = if nil?(rows) then reverse(seen) else nt-tried-go(rows[1:], aspect, if (((String) nt-row-str(rows[0], "stage") == "applied") && ((String) nt-row-str(rows[0], "aspect") == aspect) && ((Comparable) nt-has(seen, nt-row-str(rows[0], "selected")) == 0)) then cons(nt-row-str(rows[0], "selected"), seen) else seen);
  def nt-comma(xs) = if nil?(xs) then "" else if nil?(xs[1:]) then xs[0] else mc-cat([xs[0], ", ", nt-comma(xs[1:])]);
  def nt-claim-line(rows, aspect) {
   let last = nt-last-observed(rows, aspect, json-node-object([]));
   let held = node_eq(json-object-get(last, "health"), json-node-int(1));
   let tried = nt-tried(rows, aspect);
   if held then "" else mc-cat(["claim ", aspect, " answered ", json-emit(json-object-get(last, "observed")), " and did not hold", if nil?(tried) then "" else mc-cat(["; the band already tried ", nt-comma(tried)]), "\n"]);
  }
  def nt-claim-lines(rows, aspects) = if nil?(aspects) then "" else ((String) nt-claim-line(rows, aspects[0]) + nt-claim-lines(rows, aspects[1:]));
  def nt-band-claims() {
   let rows = nt-band-rows(split-on(nt-read(nt-err()), "\n"));
   trim(nt-claim-lines(rows, nt-aspects(rows, [])));
  }
  // who began this turn
  def nt-row-of(value) = if ((String) value_kind(value) == "int") then [] else value;
  def nt-self() = nt-row-of(host_process(host_pid()));
  def nt-parent(me) = if (len(me) < 2) then [] else nt-row-of(host_process(me[1]));
  def nt-exe(row) = if (len(row) < 3) then "" else row[2];
  def nt-tail(path, i) = if (i <= 0) then path else if ((Comparable) str_byte_at(path, (i - 1)) == 47) then substring(path, i, len(path)) else nt-tail(path, (i - 1));
  def nt-base(path) = if ((String) path == "") then "" else nt-tail(path, len(path));
  def nt-glue?(exe) = (((String) nt-base(exe) == "fkwu") || (((String) nt-base(exe) == "sh") || (((String) nt-base(exe) == "zsh") || (((String) nt-base(exe) == "bash") || ((String) nt-base(exe) == "form-run")))));
  def nt-climb(row, hops) = if ((len(row) < 3) || (hops <= 0)) then row else if nt-glue?(nt-exe(row)) then nt-climb(nt-parent(row), (hops - 1)) else row;
  def nt-coordinator() = nt-exe(nt-climb(nt-parent(nt-self()), 8));
  def nt-keeper?(exe) = ((String) nt-base(exe) == "launchd");
  // the request the native code lane reads
  def nt-doc(path) = json-node-object([fhn-s("id",path),fhn-s("path",path),fhn-s("text",fhn-read(path))]);
  def nt-docs(paths) = if nil?(paths) then [] else cons(nt-doc(paths[0]), nt-docs(paths[1:]));
  def nt-strings(xs) = if nil?(xs) then [] else cons(json-node-string(xs[0]), nt-strings(xs[1:]));
  // every writable file keeps the paren and brace balance it had before the lane (the lane's read-only balance tool)
  def nt-count(text, i, n, open, close, d) = if (i >= n) then d else nt-count(text, (i + 1), n, open, close, if ((Comparable) str_byte_at(text, i) == open) then (d + 1) else if ((Comparable) str_byte_at(text, i) == close) then (d - 1) else d);
  def nt-balance-text(text) = mc-cat([nt-count(text, 0, len(text), 40, 41, 0).str(), " ", nt-count(text, 0, len(text), 123, 125, 0).str(), "\n"]);
  def nt-balance(path) = json-node-object([fhn-s("tool", "balance"), json-node-pair("arguments", json-node-array([json-node-string(path)])), fhn-s("stdout", nt-balance-text(fhn-read(path)))]);
